  "english": "December\n\n4. Sunday. Tone 4 [Dadz, ԴՁ]. Second [Sunday of Advent]. [Resurrection] Canticle of the Fathers, Tone 3 [Pez, ԲՁ / ԲԿ]: \"Incorruptible\" (Anapakan). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 4 [Dadz, ԴՁ], third: \"You who are in the heights\" (Vor i verd es).\n\n5. Monday. Tone 8 [Diuk, ԴԿ]. [Feast of Saints] Gennarios, and Mercurius, and James, and Iravap'ar.\n\n6. Tuesday. Tone 1 [Ats, ԱՁ]. [Feast of] Abgar the King. The Scripture readings and Gospel are those of Theodosius.\n\n9. Friday. Tone 4 [Pek, ԲԿ]. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Mother of God from Anna.\n\n11. Sunday. Tone 6 [Kadz, ԳԿ]. Third [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers, Tone 6 [Kadz, ԳԿ]: \"God without beginning\" (Anskizbn astuats). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 6 [Kadz, ԳԿ]: \"Taking and ours\" (Areal yev mer). Fast-break [Eve] of the Fast of Saint James.\n\n14. Wednesday. Tone 1 [Ats, ԱՁ]. Canticle of the Fathers for Fasting, Tone 4: \"Who for the three youths\" (Vor zeris mankunsn).\n\n18. Sunday. Tone 5 [Gadz, ԳՁ]. Fourth [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers, Tone 5 [Gadz, ԳՁ]: \"Glorified Son\" (Paravorial vordi). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 5 [Gadz, ԳՁ]: \"Myrrh-bearing\" (Yughaber), to the end.\n\n24. Saturday. Tone 3 [Padz, ԲՁ]. [Feast of] David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n\n25. Sunday. Tone 4 [Pek, ԲԿ]. Fifth [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers, Tone 5 [Gadz, ԳՁ]: \"Before eternity\" (Nakhayavitean). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 4 [Pek, ԲԿ]: \"They anticipated\" (Kankhetsin), to the end.\n\n29. Thursday. Tone 8 [Diuk, ԴԿ]. [Feast of] the Sons of Thunder, James and John. Fast-break [Eve] of the Fast of the Nativity.\n\n31. Saturday. Tone 2 [Aks, ԱԿ]. Fast day. [Feast of] the Patriarchs Basil, and others.\n\nJanuary\n\n1. Sunday. Tone 3 [Padz, ԲՁ]. Sixth [Sunday of Advent]. Fast day. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 3 [Padz, ԲՁ]: \"Today they rejoiced\" (Aysor zuarchatsan), to the end.\n\n2. Monday. Tone 4 [Pek, ԲԿ]. Fast day. Canticle of the Fathers, Tone 8 [Diuk, ԴԿ]: \"[God of] our fathers\" (Hartsën merots).\n\n5. Thursday. Tone 7 [Dadz, ԴՁ]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ [Theophany].\n\nTHE SEVEN-DAY CYCLE OF THE ROMANS 5.\n\n23. Saturday. [Feast of] the Patriarchs Athanasius and Cyril.\n\n24. Sunday. Second [Sunday]. Canticle of the Fathers, Tone 6 [Kadz, ԳԿ]: \"Today he became...\"\n\n25. Monday. [Feast of] Vahan of Goghtn.\n\n26. Tuesday. [Feast of] Eugine the Virgin, and her father Philip, and others.\n\n28. Thursday. [Feast of] Eugenius, Macarius, and others.\n\n30. Saturday. [Feast of] Gregory the Theologian.\n\n31. Sunday. Third [Sunday]. Fast-break [Eve] of the Fast of the Catechumens [Arachavorats]. See the order and the rest in the First Volume up to Transfiguration, keeping the order of this place.\n\nFebruary\n\n7. Sunday. [Feast of] Saint Sargis. Canticle of the Fathers, Tone 8 [Diuk, ԴԿ]: \"Who with awesome form\" (Vor aheghakerp).\n\nJanuary\n\n6. WEDNESDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Theophany of Christ. The period of non-fasting days [eating days] is twenty-six days.\n\n14. Thursday. [Feast of] John the Forerunner.\n\n16. Saturday. [Feast of] Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and others.\n\n17. Sunday. First [Sunday after Theophany]. Canticle of the Fathers, Tone 7 [Dadz, ԴՁ]: \"The dawning of the Only-begotten\" (Tsagumn miatsni).\n\n18. Monday. [Feast of] Antony, and Triphon, Parsam, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n\n19. Tuesday. [Feast of] Theodosius the King, and the Holy Infants of Ephesus.\n\n21. Thursday. [Feast of] Cyriacus and Julietta, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris.",
